<<is_defaultable_typeIR, ``typeIR''`` can be default-initialized>>:
[cols="2", options="header"]
|===
| (``typeIR''``) | Result 

| BOOL | true
| ERROR | true
| STRING | true
| integerTypeIR | true
| TYPEDEF ++_++ typeIR | <<is_defaultable_typeIR, is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)>>
| TYPE ++_++ typeIR | <<is_defaultable_typeIR, is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)>>
| TUPLE < typeIR^{asterisk}^ > | <<forall_, forall_(is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)^{asterisk}^)>>
| typeIR [ ++_++ ] | <<is_defaultable_typeIR, is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)>>
| STRUCT ++_++ < ++_++^{asterisk}^ > { ( ++_++ typeIR ++_++ ; )^{asterisk}^ } | <<forall_, forall_(is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)^{asterisk}^)>>
| HEADER ++_++ < ++_++^{asterisk}^ > { ( ++_++ typeIR ++_++ ; )^{asterisk}^ } | <<forall_, forall_(is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)^{asterisk}^)>>
| HEADER_UNION ++_++ < ++_++^{asterisk}^ > { ( ++_++ typeIR ++_++ ; )^{asterisk}^ } | <<forall_, forall_(is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)^{asterisk}^)>>
| ENUM ++_++ { ++_++^{asterisk}^ } | true
| ENUM ++_++ < typeIR > { ++_++^{asterisk}^ } | <<is_defaultable_typeIR, is_defaultable_typeIR(typeIR)>>
| ++_++ | false

|===

<<is_equalable_typeIR, ``typeIR''`` supports equality comparison>>:
[cols="2", options="header"]
|===
| (``typeIR''``) | Result 

| VOID | false
| typeId | false
| TYPEDEF ++_++ typeIR | <<is_equalable_typeIR, is_equalable_typeIR(typeIR)>>
| externObjectTypeIR | false
| parserObjectTypeIR | false
| controlObjectTypeIR | false
| packageObjectTypeIR | false
| tableObjectTypeIR | false
| DEFAULT | false
| SEQ < ++_++^{asterisk}^ , ... > | false
| RECORD { ++_++^{asterisk}^ , ... } | false
| HEADER_INVALID | false
| setTypeIR | false
| tableMetadataTypeIR | false
| ++_++ | true

|===

<<is_assignable_typeIR, ``typeIR''`` supports assignment>>:
[cols="2", options="header"]
|===
| (``typeIR''``) | Result 

| VOID | false
| STRING | false
| INT | false
| TYPEDEF ++_++ typeIR | <<is_assignable_typeIR, is_assignable_typeIR(typeIR)>>
